From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:36:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07686/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-WMTE-5830: goal verifier
 tuning -- completion signal + aligned patience

First goal-verify run (v4) showed the mechanism works (sc25 falsified
a goal, model switched) but fired too rarely: goal_patience=24 >>
reflection_interval=10, so goals get reworded (counter resets) before
the patience window is met. Two fixes: (1) the DEFINITIVE signal from
the winner-recipe failure -- falsify when the model's PROGRESS reports
it COMPLETED the goal (bp35: "column 63 filled") yet no level-up fired
(progress_indicates_completion + falsify_on_reported_completion); (2)
lower goal_patience 24->12, min_activity 6->4 to fire within a
reflection cycle. 4 new tests (38 total, mypy clean).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
